  "facts": [
    "The William Jolly Bridge, completed in 1932, was the first rainbow arch bridge in Australia, featuring three graceful steel arches with a concrete veneer designed to mimic light‑coloured porphyry.",
    "Opened during the Great Depression, the bridge was initially called the Grey Street Bridge before being renamed on 5 July 1955 to honor William Jolly, Brisbane's inaugural Lord Mayor.",
    "Designed by Harding Frew and constructed by MR Hornibrook, the bridge spans the Brisbane River between North Quay in the CBD and Grey Street in South Brisbane, linking the city’s commercial heart to its southern precinct."
